{"id": "p02", "domain": "pain", "procedure": "THA", "answerability": "full", "model": "gemma3:4b", "model_digest": "a2af6cc3eb7fa8be8504abaf9b04e88f17a119ec3f04a3addf55f92841195f5a", "variant": "project", "project_layout": "system_user", "status": "ok", "error": null, "response": "It’s completely normal to still have some pain and stiffness in your hip after your surgery, and it’s common for this to fluctuate, especially around your medication times. We’ve focused on managing this with scheduled pain relief and encouraging you to elevate your leg and ice it to help reduce swelling, but it’s important to remember that pain levels can vary and should be reported to the surgical team if they become concerning.", "response_sha256": "117b1fec68d53b1509b09a6f41c9815996ca0433c268bca0742d48e0bb4b9c43", "empty_response": false, "thinking": null, "done_reason": "stop", "latency_s": {"first_chunk": 0.3858302000153344, "first_token": 0.3858302000153344, "first_thinking": null, "total": 2.030534899997292}, "ollama_timings": {"total_duration_ns": 2029146100, "load_duration_ns": 7021400, "prompt_eval_count": 734, "prompt_eval_duration_ns": 329329000, "eval_count": 87, "eval_duration_ns": 1644690000, "eval_tokens_per_s": 52.9}, "memory": {"gpu_used_at_start_mib": 3731, "gpu_used_peak_mib": 3731, "ollama_process_peak_mib": 92.5, "ollama_process_method": "psutil_rss", "sample_interval_s": 0.25, "samples": 5, "loaded_model": {"size_bytes": 2875520450, "size_vram_bytes": 2875520450}}, "options": {"temperature": 0, "num_predict": 300, "seed": 0, "num_ctx": 4096}, "think": null, "prompt_sha256": "c344d4a6e101fcfba0793d7fa64188c697389f4d1b5e30973ea98b00566340fe", "context_sha256": "f6f6ad54a63d11878b8dc3680a72dfaaee6b0b0c97d19a44c98e7a9c8744e233", "corpus": {"kind": "rag_store_copy", "path": "rag/data/seed_knowledge.json", "sha256": "35996f41a8bce0a2bd43920c44347b340481f0da120eebb855255c02c1af9e94"}, "query_sha256": "d75d1a2cd4f00a645d80e19bf45b1cd7967276f7e767e2c4e861fd9d36dd0924", "postop_day": 7, "n_context_chunks": 4, "prompt_chars": 3512, "context_may_be_truncated": false, "started_at": "2026-09-28T09:33:46+00:00", "finished_at": "2026-09-28T09:33:48+00:00", "harness_version": "1"}
{"id": "p03", "domain": "pain", "procedure": "TKA", "answerability": "partial", "model": "gemma3:4b", "model_digest": "a2af6cc3eb7fa8be8504abaf9b04e88f17a119ec3f04a3addf55f92841195f5a", "variant": "project", "project_layout": "system_user", "status": "ok", "error": null, "response": "It’s common for pain to fluctuate, especially at night after a TKA. Since you’re experiencing increased pain at night, try elevating your leg above your heart level and applying ice to the knee – this can really help reduce swelling and discomfort. Remember to take your scheduled acetaminophen as directed, and if you notice any concerning signs like persistent pain or swelling that doesn’t improve with these measures, please let your surgical team know right away.", "response_sha256": "141c61f629f1b917656632f2dd040b84a73838093b76885142ff3f0a76713bcb", "empty_response": false, "thinking": null, "done_reason": "stop", "latency_s": {"first_chunk": 0.43199720000848174, "first_token": 0.43199720000848174, "first_thinking": null, "total": 2.160541599994758}, "ollama_timings": {"total_duration_ns": 2159515400, "load_duration_ns": 7351300, "prompt_eval_count": 738, "prompt_eval_duration_ns": 337006000, "eval_count": 91, "eval_duration_ns": 1728778000, "eval_tokens_per_s": 52.64}, "memory": {"gpu_used_at_start_mib": 3731, "gpu_used_peak_mib": 3731, "ollama_process_peak_mib": 92.6, "ollama_process_method": "psutil_rss", "sample_interval_s": 0.25, "samples": 5, "loaded_model": {"size_bytes": 2875520450, "size_vram_bytes": 2875520450}}, "options": {"temperature": 0, "num_predict": 300, "seed": 0, "num_ctx": 4096}, "think": null, "prompt_sha256": "3af04f7df9bdd1444d543e1feda3e026073cf31043382c4dbaf9c56761e696e3", "context_sha256": "09651659ac9c575f105555474853cf1432151d0c647b44720c5309b9e37673ca", "corpus": {"kind": "rag_store_copy", "path": "rag/data/seed_knowledge.json", "sha256": "35996f41a8bce0a2bd43920c44347b340481f0da120eebb855255c02c1af9e94"}, "query_sha256": "62f8ba72620e102385fa008f568588284fa1d409742902a9850b88d6bad0039e", "postop_day": 21, "n_context_chunks": 4, "prompt_chars": 3551, "context_may_be_truncated": false, "started_at": "2026-09-28T09:33:48+00:00", "finished_at": "2026-09-28T09:33:50+00:00", "harness_version": "1"}
{"id": "p04", "domain": "pain", "procedure": "THA", "answerability": "none", "model": "gemma3:4b", "model_digest": "a2af6cc3eb7fa8be8504abaf9b04e88f17a119ec3f04a3addf55f92841195f5a", "variant": "project", "project_layout": "system_user", "status": "ok", "error": null, "response": "It’s great you’re thinking about managing your pain, but **absolutely do not take ibuprofen with your blood thinner.** The discharge notes clearly state that combining NSAIDs like ibuprofen with blood thinners can significantly increase your risk of bleeding. Stick to the medications prescribed for you and always report any unusual symptoms like bruising or black stools to your surgical team right away.", "response_sha256": "75daa5390194d714014468660c4d9af159ffb271ceaaeffb778b4fee286f96e1", "empty_response": false, "thinking": null, "done_reason": "stop", "latency_s": {"first_chunk": 0.3304520999954548, "first_token": 0.3304520999954548, "first_thinking": null, "total": 1.7238162999856286}, "ollama_timings": {"total_duration_ns": 1722550400, "load_duration_ns": 6488400, "prompt_eval_count": 494, "prompt_eval_duration_ns": 231511000, "eval_count": 74, "eval_duration_ns": 1393298000, "eval_tokens_per_s": 53.11}, "memory": {"gpu_used_at_start_mib": 3731, "gpu_used_peak_mib": 3731, "ollama_process_peak_mib": 92.6, "ollama_process_method": "psutil_rss", "sample_interval_s": 0.25, "samples": 5, "loaded_model": {"size_bytes": 2875520450, "size_vram_bytes": 2875520450}}, "options": {"temperature": 0, "num_predict": 300, "seed": 0, "num_ctx": 4096}, "think": null, "prompt_sha256": "59b3e2d2c0eb9ab10e62ce2abfd0bf15e05ddb4e298b3d5b6232338c3b7d202c", "context_sha256": "fac6738eca2096ab6aebbbf3eeed1b5384648a380d9ab03c1d8383e43a9d2ad1", "corpus": {"kind": "rag_store_copy", "path": "rag/data/seed_knowledge.json", "sha256": "35996f41a8bce0a2bd43920c44347b340481f0da120eebb855255c02c1af9e94"}, "query_sha256": "ce238b2891d9cb4de21c537e32a8078986dc63c1c980cc4b056f74d8ded3e29e", "postop_day": 42, "n_context_ch